+# v436 PF (ours, 2026-09-26; results/v436/BRIEF.md, PASTURE.md): re-issue a weed-blocked pasture / coop build.
+# _weed_repair turns a tape BUILD_PASTURE / BUILD_COOP on a WEED into a DIG and queues the build, but replays the
+# queue only while the unit's next tape command is a no-op. When the tape walks the unit on (the opening's (4,2)
+# pasture: DIG at step 33, SOUTH at 34) the queue is dropped a step later, the pasture is never built and the cow
+# bought for it waits in the shed to the end (results/v434/CENSUS.md, g104). When _pf_trigger holds, the unit
+# builds at the first legal step (the next one: the DIG left the tile empty and the unit still stands on it), then
+# plays its own tape one step late until a delayed command is a PASS, which it drops to rejoin the tape; the lag
+# ends at the day boundary. The mechanism follows the weed lag replay (_e343_weedlag) of evgendvorkin's public
+# Kaggle notebook "Kaggriculture" (Apache-2.0 notices in that file), re-implemented here inside the chassis so that
+# every outer layer sees the corrected command stream. While _pf_trigger never holds, the chassis output is the
+# base's own, byte for byte (state is written only when it fires).
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+_PF_OPS = ("BUILD_PASTURE", "BUILD_COOP")
+_PF_WEED_REPAIR = Chassis._weed_repair
